# Stack contract

lex-flow hosts **UI8Kit** on Svelte 5. The kit owns atoms, recipes, and tag
groups. The app owns session, copy, routing, and transport. Product kinds
stay out of the kit.

Paths below are relative to the `app/` package root.

- One kit, one app shell, many screens. Do not add a second CSS system or a
  parallel widget tree.
- The host runtime is Svelte. Recipes (`*.variants.json`), `*.shared.ts`,
  and `src/kit/utils` stay shared.
- Screens compose kit bricks. They do not invent host paths, disk layout, or
  a second content API.
- Product variation is copy, tokens, and view composition.
- `@ui8kit/codegen` emits hosts. Do not hand-edit generated brick files.
- Kit and `.cursor/rules` are copyable. lex-flow types stay in the app
  (`src/lib`), never in `src/kit`.
